> [!WARNING]
> **`replaceIdentifier` renames an `AS`-less table alias, corrupting the FROM and `$__orgFilter`**
>
> <sub>F3 · Warning · correctness</sub>

`definedNames` records only `AS x`, `x AS (` and CTE names, so a table alias declared without `AS` is unprotected while `replaceIdentifier` rewrites every occurrence of the rejected name. `SELECT service FROM traces service WHERE $__orgFilter(service)` comes back as `SELECT ServiceName FROM traces ServiceName WHERE $__orgFilter(ServiceName)`: invalid SQL, and an org filter that names no table, so the rerun fails on an error the agent never wrote.

```
Also decline the rewrite when `tableQualifiers(sql)` maps the rejected name as a qualifier, next to the `definedNames(sql)` check.
```

```suggestion
	const written = unknownIdentifierName(message)
	const qualifiers = tableQualifiers(sql)
	// A table alias is a name the query defines: renaming it breaks the FROM and the
	// `$__orgFilter(...)` that names it.
	if (written === undefined || definedNames(sql).has(written) || qualifiers.has(written))
		return undefined
	const to = identifierFix(written, referencedTables(sql), qualifiers)
```
